---
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About · CODEDNA';
const description =
  'CODEDNA is a technology + biology company exploring the intersection of computation, technology, and biological systems.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container-page">
      <h1 class="text-h1 hero__title">About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The short version: CODEDNA is a technology + biology company. The slightly longer
        version is below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 01 · The company -->
  <Section id="company" index="01" rule>
    <SectionHeading
      label="The company"
      title="Two disciplines, one company"
    />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        CODEDNA happens where software, computation, and engineering meet living systems — in
        their measurement, in their data, and in the laboratory.
      </p>
      <p>
        The company is deliberately small and deliberately early. Its offering, if any, is
        still being defined. What exists today is a point of view, a discipline, and a
        decision to work where two fields refuse to stay separate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- 02 · The name -->
  <Section id="name" index="02" rule>
    <SectionHeading
      label="The name"
      title="CODE plus DNA"
    />
    <p class="name-lockup" aria-hidden="true">
      CODE&thinsp;+&thinsp;DNA
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The name is the concatenation. Code is our home discipline — software understood as
        precision, structure, and method. DNA stands for the biological half — living systems,
        measured and engineered. The name binds the two without pretending they are the same
        thing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- 03 · Why the seam -->
  <Section id="why" index="03" rule>
    <SectionHeading
      label="Why the seam"
      title="Biology became a data problem"
    />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Biology now produces measurements at a scale that software was built for, and
        computation has become a way to work on living systems directly. Neither field finishes
        the job on its own.
      </p>
      <p>
        The instruments, protocols, and code that connect them are some of the least polished
        parts of modern science — and some of the most consequential.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- 04 · Mission & philosophy -->
  <Section id="mission" index="04" rule>
    <SectionHeading
      label="Mission and manner"
      title="Measured before announced"
    />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Our direction: to make working on biological systems with code as ordinary as working
        on systems of any other kind.
      </p>
      <p>
        In manner: rigor from engineering, patience from biology, and work that is measured
        before it is announced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- 05 · Current status -->
  <Section id="status" index="05" rule tone="surface">
    <SectionHeading
      label="Current status"
      title="Where we are right now"
    />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        CODEDNA is in an exploratory phase. There is no polished offering to announce, no
        roadmap to sell, and no capability claimed that has not been demonstrated.
      </p>
      <p>
        As the direction firms up, this site will be the first place it shows.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- 06 · Contact -->
  <CallToAction index="06" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 12vw, 7.5rem) clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6rem);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .hero__title {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero .lede {
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .name-lockup {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 2.5vw + 1rem, 3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }
</style>